xDripX changes
==============

Scope
-----

This file describes the changes in the supplied diff relative to:

    baseline: 9898cb8e08b3a06226e62e35b75849891074c830
    HEAD:     c71f9715498e4103e31cf9ce617be41f28a7b672

It describes functional changes rather than reproducing the patch line by line.

1. Separate xDripX debug build
-----------------------------

Files:
    app/build.gradle
    app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml
    app/src/debug/google-services.json
    wear/build.gradle
    build_and_run.sh

The development build is now deliberately distinct from the normal xDrip+
installation.

- The phone debug build gets the application-ID suffix ".debug", allowing it
  to coexist with the normal com.eveningoutpost.dexdrip installation.
- The displayed application name is controlled by the Gradle project property
  "appName", with "xDrip+" as the fallback.

  Why? To allow both apps to run on the same device (i.e. phone) and be
  clearly distinct.
  
- build_and_run.sh sets APP_NAME="xDripX" and passes it to the phone build.

- app_name, app_name_launcher and the Android application label derive from
  this build-time name rather than being permanently hard-coded.

- The Wear module uses the same appName property for its application,
  complication and settings labels, including names such as:
      xDripX
      xDripX(Large)
      xDripX(BigChart)
      xDripX(Circle)
      xDripX Prefs.
      xDripX Settings
      
- The Wear debug build also receives the ".debug" application-ID suffix.

- A debug google-services.json has been added for
  com.eveningoutpost.dexdrip.debug.
  
- Minification and resource shrinking are disabled for the phone debug build,
  making the test build easier to debug.

2. Newer Android compatibility
------------------------------

Files:
    app/build.gradle
    app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/GcmListenerSvc.java
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/Home.java
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/MegaStatus.java
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/Reminders.java
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/cloud/backup/BackupActivity.java
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/models/JoH.java
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/services/ActivityRecognizedService.java
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/services/DailyIntentService.java
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/services/DexShareCollectionService.java
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/services/G5CollectionService.java
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/services/MissedReadingService.java
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/services/Ob1G5CollectionService.java
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/services/SyncService.java
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/utilitymodels/AlertPlayer.java
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/utilitymodels/CollectionServiceStarter.java
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/utilitymodels/Notifications.java
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/utils/CheckBridgeBattery.java
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/utils/framework/WakeLockTrampoline.java
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/wearintegration/WatchUpdaterService.java
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/xDripWidget.java
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/xDripWidgetExtended.java

The phone build has been updated for newer Android behaviour, particularly the
Android 12+ Bluetooth, component-export and PendingIntent rules encountered on
the Android 16 test phone.

- targetSdkVersion is increased from 26 to 32.
- RxAndroidBle is updated from 1.12.1 to 1.19.1.
- Legacy BLUETOOTH and BLUETOOTH_ADMIN permissions are retained only through
  API 30.
- BLUETOOTH_SCAN and BLUETOOTH_CONNECT are declared explicitly.
- BLUETOOTH_SCAN is marked neverForLocation.
- Components with intent filters that must be externally reachable now have
  explicit android:exported declarations. This includes the launcher activity,
  widget receivers and a number of system/integration receivers and services.
- PendingIntents throughout the application are explicitly marked immutable
  where appropriate. This includes notifications, scheduled services,
  broadcasts and widget click actions.
- The xDrip widgets therefore use explicit immutable click PendingIntents and
  explicitly exported widget receivers under the newer Android rules.

3. Dexcom ONE+ / short-transmitter BLE connection strategy
----------------------------------------------------------

Files:
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/services/Ob1G5CollectionService.java
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/g5model/Ob1G5StateMachine.java
    wear/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/services/Ob1G5CollectionService.java

The largest behavioural change is a separate, more conservative BLE path for
short transmitter IDs, logged in the code as ONE+.

3.1 Always scan for ONE+

The normal "minimise scanning" direct-connect optimisation is disabled for
short transmitter IDs.

- ONE+ performs a real BLE scan rather than relying on a previously saved MAC
  address and direct reconnect.
- The general minimise-scanning strategy now also requires a locally bonded
  device and rejects the direct-connect path after a pre-scan failure.
- A saved transmitter MAC is still used where appropriate for other
  transmitters.
- When a MAC is already known, the phone now enters CONNECT_NOW rather than
  CONNECT.
- The Wear collector has the same CONNECT -> CONNECT_NOW change. This has
  not been tested: my test setup has the watch simply mirroring the phone's
  readings.

The intention is to avoid repeated bad direct connections on the newer phone
Bluetooth stack.

3.2 Detect and abandon slow GATT setup

For ONE+, setup of the ExtraData notification and Authentication indication is
timed.

- A setup taking more than 1500 ms is treated as a slow GATT connection.
- A BleCannotSetCharacteristicNotificationException during these setup stages
  is also treated as a connection that should be abandoned.
- Rather than continuing on a connection that is already behaving badly,
  xDripX closes/disposes the connection, marks the failure as requiring a real
  scan and starts a new scan after the subscriptions have unwound.
- recoverFromSlowGatt() keeps the state at CLOSE while teardown occurs and
  moves back to SCAN after a one-second delay.

This is intended to recover quickly from the characteristic-setup stalls seen
with ONE+ instead of allowing the session to fail later during authentication
or data transfer.

3.3 ONE+ authentication/KEKS recovery

Authentication handling now recognises the three-byte response 05 02 01 as a
rejected KEKS authentication.

When this happens, xDripX:

- marks authentication as failed
- clears both persisted and live KEKS state
- discards the current KEKS plugin instance
- removes the stale Android Bluetooth bond
- resets collector state
- waits before retrying so Android and the transmitter can finish tearing down
  the old bond/connection

This allows a fresh KEKS exchange and bond to be established rather than
repeatedly retrying an invalid saved key/bond combination.

3.4 Notification rather than indication for the ONE+ control channel

For short transmitter IDs, the Control characteristic is set up with
setupNotification() rather than setupIndication().

Other transmitter types retain the existing indication path.

Control-channel notification setup failures on ONE+ use the same clean
slow-GATT recovery path rather than forcing work to continue on the failed
connection.

3.5 Prefer a high-priority BLE connection

After a ONE+ connection is established, xDripX asks Android for
BluetoothGatt.CONNECTION_PRIORITY_HIGH.

Failure to obtain high priority is logged but does not itself abort the
connection.

3.6 Protect the state machine from stale asynchronous callbacks

Several guards have been added to prevent late callbacks from an old BLE
operation from changing the state of a newer connection attempt.

- Scan results are ignored unless the collector is still in SCAN.
- Service-discovery results are ignored unless the collector is still in
  DISCOVER.
- A scheduled service wake-up is ignored for ONE+ when a recently connected
  session is already actively progressing through discovery, authentication,
  bonding/unbonding or data collection.

These changes reduce races between asynchronous BLE callbacks and the collector
state machine.

3.7 Force a real scan after characteristic setup failures

A preScanFailureMarker is set when relevant characteristic
notification/indication setup fails.

That marker prevents the minimise-scanning/direct-connect path on the next
attempt, forcing a fresh scan instead.

3.8 Safer saved transmitter MAC handling

saveTransmitterMac() now refuses to persist a MAC address unless both the
transmitter ID and MAC are present and the MAC has the expected 17-character
form.

This prevents a failed or partial scan from poisoning the saved direct-connect
state.

4. Backfill handling
--------------------

File:
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/g5model/Ob1G5StateMachine.java

The backfill check no longer blindly asks for the configured number of recent
readings when the sensor/transmitter has not existed for that long.

- The effective start time is calculated from the sensor start and known
  transmitter start.
- The number of readings that can actually exist since that time is calculated.
- The backfill check size is capped to that available number.
- Logging reports the requested and available check sizes.

This avoids asking the database/backfill logic to examine more history than can
exist for a newly started sensor/transmitter.

5. Collector diagnostics
------------------------

File:
    app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/services/Ob1G5CollectionService.java

The collector status now permanently shows "Last Data Received" rather than
only showing the old native-algorithm item for a short period.

The status includes:

- the time of the last usable glucose packet
- how long ago it was received
- GOOD highlighting below 7 minutes
- NOTICE highlighting from 7 to 15 minutes
- BAD highlighting after 15 minutes

Connection-failure logging has also been expanded to show both normal-connect
and CONNECT_NOW failure metrics.

Additional recovery/debug helpers expose the current error count, clear KEKS
state for retry and provide a rate-limited Bluetooth-restart helper.

6. Wear OS changes
------------------

Files:
    wear/build.gradle
    wear/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/services/Ob1G5CollectionService.java

- Wear targetSdkVersion is increased from 23 to 24 for the Galaxy Watch 4
  test environment.
- The Wear debug application gets the ".debug" application-ID suffix.
- Wear labels follow the same build-time appName property as the phone build.
- When the Wear collector already knows the transmitter MAC it uses
  CONNECT_NOW rather than CONNECT. This has not been tested: my test setup has
  the watch simply mirroring the phone's readings.




7. Local build, install and debugging workflow
----------------------------------------------

Files:
    build_and_run.sh
    my_private_details.sh.example
    .gitignore
    README

A reproducible local test workflow has been added.

build_and_run.sh:

- finds the repository relative to the script itself
- reads device-specific details from my_private_details.sh
- keeps phone and watch adb targets together as arrays
- builds the phone and Wear APKs
- installs the test APKs
- enables the phone debug package
- stops normal xDrip, Juggluco and xDripX before testing
- clears logcat
- launches the xDripX debug package
- displays a filtered BLE/authentication log suitable for testing the ONE+
  connection path

my_private_details.sh.example contains placeholders for:

- PHONE_SERIAL
- WATCH_ADDRESS

Note: 
The Wear APK is installed automatically if the configured watch is reachable
and available through ADB; otherwise watch installation is skipped.

The real my_private_details.sh is excluded by .gitignore.

README documents the phone/watch test setup, build/install commands, Bluetooth
restart commands and useful filtered logcat command.

8. Test devices documented
---------------------------

The new README records the environment used for this work:

- Sony Xperia 1 VII running Android 16
- Samsung Galaxy Watch 4 connected using Wi-Fi ADB debugging

Tested on Ubuntu Linux 24.04 running Android Debug Bridge version 1.0.41, Version 34.0.4-debian, Installed as /usr/lib/android-sdk/platform-tools/adb, Running on Linux 6.8.0-142-generic (x86_64)

This was developed on a laptop bought on STFC grant ST/R000603/1.
Yes, it's an old device, but thanks STFC - you're literally life savers!

